description:
FILED s521c (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-18) from the #1576 one-file acceptance run of Mojo-DOM58 t/collection.t (subtest 'first', its row 6 "right result").

A List::Util block function's BLOCK sees the ENCLOSING sub's @_ in perl (the XS calls the block with MULTICALL, no new @_); PCL's block is a lambda with an empty @_.

REPRO (probed, perl 5.40.3 vs PCL on 0b836815 + s521c):
    use List::Util;
    sub f { my $x = shift; return List::Util::first { print "args=@_\n"; 1 } (1,2); }
    f('x', 'A', 'B');
perl: args=A B      PCL: args=

REACH: Mojo::DOM58::_Collection::first is `return List::Util::first { $_->$cb(@_) } @$self;` -- `$collection->first(first => sub {...})` passes the trailing code ref through @_; PCL calls ->first with no args.  Board: Mojo-DOM58 collection.t row 6 "first" (child row 6).
Layer: the block-call mechanism of the List::Util shim / the runtime's block-arg call (the #1286 family: perl sets $_ and passes NOTHING -- and the enclosing @_ stays visible).
